# THE SIFREI ROWS on Deuteronomy 3:23-29 (THE DEUTERONOMY WALK sitting 1 — THE OPENING SPEECH, 2026-09-15): piskaot 26-30 by POSITION — on
# 3:23 (26, ten rows), 3:24 (27, no citation at its head), 3:25 (28), 3:26-28 (29), 3:29 (30); thirty-one rows, each read in both files;
# the middah named. The shelf's Hebrew cut by consonants (deu_ink.SP_). Piska 31 opens at 6:4 — the span's last piska is 30.
from deu_ink import *
S = {}
def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

srow(26, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND I BESOUGHT THE LORD AT THAT TIME, SAYING" — THIS IS WHAT SCRIPTURE SAYS: "THE POOR SPEAKS SUPPLICATIONS, THE RICH ANSWERS ROUGHLY" (Proverbs 18:23). The head row on 3:23 ({SP_(26, 1, "תחנונים", "ידבר", "רש")} "the poor speaks supplications") — the hapax verb (the ink) read by its noun in Proverbs: Moses the poor man pleading.')
srow(26, 2, 'CONTEXT', 'TWO GOOD PROVIDERS AROSE FOR ISRAEL, MOSES AND DAVID. MOSES: LET MY SIN BE WRITTEN AFTER ME, LEST THEY SAY MOSES FORGED THE TORAH — THE PARABLE OF THE WOMAN WHO ATE UNRIPE SABBATICAL FIGS AND ASKED THAT HER FAULT BE PROCLAIMED; THE HOLY ONE: I WRITE IT — IT WAS ONLY AT THE WATER ("AS YOU REBELLED AGAINST MY WORD", Numbers 27:14). Moses\' sin recorded (the English notes 26:2-6 thought a late addition).')
srow(26, 3, 'CONTEXT', 'R. SHIMON: THE KING WHOSE CARRIAGE OVERTURNED ON HIS SON AT A NARROW PLACE — HERE HIS EYE WAS BLINDED, HIS HAND CUT, HIS LEG BROKEN; SO THE OMNIPRESENT MENTIONS THE WATERS OF MERIBAH THREE TIMES: HERE I KILLED MIRIAM, AARON, MOSES ("THEIR JUDGES ARE THROWN DOWN BY THE ROCK", Psalm 141:6). The three Meribahs.')
srow(26, 4, 'CONTEXT', 'DAVID: LET MY SIN NOT BE WRITTEN AFTER ME; THE OMNIPRESENT: IT IS NOT FITTING — THEY WOULD SAY HE FORGAVE HIM FOR LOVE; THE PARABLE OF THE BORROWER OF A THOUSAND KOR WHOSE CHILDREN WERE SOLD; DAVID\'S PUNISHMENTS DOUBLED — "FOURFOLD" (2 Samuel 12:6), R. HANINA: SIXTEEN. David\'s sin recorded.')
srow(26, 5, 'CONTEXT', 'NATHAN REBUKED HIM; DAVID: "I HAVE SINNED AGAINST THE LORD" (2 Samuel 12:13); "THE LORD HAS PUT AWAY YOUR SIN"; "AGAINST YOU ALONE HAVE I SINNED" (Psalm 51:6). David\'s confession.')
srow(26, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'TWO GOOD PROVIDERS, MOSES AND DAVID, COULD HAVE HUNG THE WORLD ON THEIR GOOD DEEDS, AND ASKED OF THE OMNIPRESENT ONLY A FREE GIFT — A FORTIORI: ONE WHO IS NOT ONE OF A THOUSAND THOUSANDS OF THEIR DISCIPLES\' DISCIPLES, HOW MUCH MORE SHOULD ASK ONLY A FREE GIFT! ({SP_(26, 6, "ולא", "בקשו", "מן", "המקום", "שיתן", "להם", "אלא")} "and they asked of the Omnipresent that he give them only") — the plea-verb read as the grace-root (a free gift): the a-fortiori (I1) from Moses to all.')
srow(26, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "AND I BESOUGHT" — PRAYER IS CALLED BY TEN NAMES: CRY, SHOUT, GROAN (Exodus 2:23-24); DISTRESS AND CALLING (2 Samuel 22:7); SONG AND ENTREATY (Jeremiah 7:16); FALLING (9:25); PRAYER (9:26); ENTREATING (Genesis 25:21); STANDING (Psalm 106:30); SEEKING (Exodus 32:11); SUPPLICATION — "AND I BESOUGHT THE LORD". THE TEN NAMES ROW ({SP_(26, 7, "עשרה", "לשונות", "נקראת", "תפלה")} "by ten expressions prayer is called") — the verb\'s hapax form the tenth name; the English counts thirteen; the compile\'s vocabulary of prayer (the effects registry\'s candidates).')
srow(26, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'"AT THAT TIME" — A PARABLE: THE PROVINCE ASKED THE KING TO MAKE IT A COLONY; WHEN TWO ENEMIES FELL BEFORE HIM THEY SAID: NOW IS THE HOUR. SO MOSES, SEEING SIHON AND OG FALL, SAID: NOW IS THE HOUR TO ASK TO ENTER THE LAND. ({SP_(26, 8, "כיון", "שראה", "שנפלו", "סיחון", "ועוג", "לפניו")} "when he saw that Sihon and Og fell before him") — \'at that time\' fixed after 3:1-22\'s victories: the plea\'s place in the sequence read by the Sifrei (the compile\'s order).')
srow(26, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'"SAYING" — ONE OF THE THINGS MOSES SAID: TELL ME WHETHER YOU WILL DO IT FOR ME OR NOT. SO "MOSES CRIED TO THE LORD, SAYING: WHAT SHALL I DO" (Exodus 17:4) — TELL ME WHETHER I FALL INTO THEIR HANDS; "MOSES SPOKE BEFORE THE LORD" (6:12) — WHETHER YOU REDEEM THEM; "HEAL HER, I PRAY" (Numbers 12:13) — WHETHER YOU HEAL; "LET THE LORD APPOINT" (27:15-16) — WHETHER YOU APPOINT LEADERS; HERE "SAYING" — TELL ME WHETHER I ENTER THE LAND. THE SUPERFLUOUS "SAYING" ({SP_(26, 9, "הודיעני", "אם", "אכנס", "לארץ", "אם", "לאו")} "tell me whether I enter the land or not") — the register\'s \'saying\' (fourteen seats in the span, the ink) read as a request for an answer at five seats; the middah: the redundancy resolved (I5).')
srow(26, 10, 'MATERIAL', f'"O LORD" (3:24) — WHEREVER "THE LORD" IS SAID, THE MEASURE OF MERCY ("THE LORD, THE LORD, GOD MERCIFUL", Exodus 34:6); WHEREVER "GOD" (ELOHIM), THE MEASURE OF JUDGMENT ("THE CAUSE OF BOTH SHALL COME BEFORE THE JUDGES", 22:8; "YOU SHALL NOT CURSE THE JUDGES", 22:27). THE TWO NAMES ROW ({SP_(26, 10, "זו", "מדת", "רחמים")} "this is the measure of mercy"; {SP_(26, 10, "זו", "מדת", "הדין")} "this is the measure of judgment") — 3:24\'s double name (the Torah\'s four seats: Abraham\'s two, Moses\' two — the ink) read as mercy addressed; the compile\'s docket: the name as an effect\'s register (THE EFFECTS LAW).')
srow(27, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU HAVE BEGUN" — YOU RELEASED MY VOW: WHEN YOU SAID "GO, BRING OUT MY PEOPLE" (Exodus 3:10) I SAID: I CANNOT, I SWORE TO JETHRO NOT TO LEAVE HIM ("MOSES SWORE TO DWELL WITH THE MAN", 2:21) — "SWORE" IS AN OATH ("SAUL ADJURED THE PEOPLE", 1 Samuel 14:24). THE ROW WITHOUT A HEAD CITATION (it continues 3:24: {SP_(27, 1, "אתה", "התרת", "לי", "נדרי")} "you released my vow for me") — \'you have begun\' read as the first release: the sages\' reading of 4:1 (\'undertaking\' an oath) applied to Moses\' own; the begin-root (the store\'s \'bore\') at its plea seat.')
srow(27, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "YOU HAVE BEGUN" — YOU OPENED ME A DOOR TO STAND AND PRAY FOR YOUR SONS AT THE CALF ("LET ME ALONE AND I WILL DESTROY THEM", 9:14) — WAS MOSES HOLDING THE HOLY ONE? RATHER: YOU OPENED THE DOOR, I PRAYED AND YOU FORGAVE; I THOUGHT I WAS WITH THEM IN PRAYER, BUT THEY DID NOT PRAY FOR ME — A FORTIORI: IF ONE MAN\'S PRAYER FOR THE MANY IS HEARD, THE MANY\'S FOR ONE HOW MUCH MORE! ({SP_(27, 2, "אתה", "פתחת", "לי", "פתח", "שאעמד", "ואתפלל")} "you opened me a door that I might stand and pray") — the a-fortiori (I1) of the many\'s prayer; \'let me alone\' read as the door.')
srow(27, 3, 'CONTEXT', '"TO SHOW YOUR SERVANT" — SOME CALLED THEMSELVES SERVANTS AND THE HOLY ONE CALLED THEM SO (ABRAHAM, JACOB, MOSES, DAVID, ISAIAH); SOME CALLED THEMSELVES SO AND HE DID NOT (SAMUEL, SAMSON, SOLOMON — HUNG ON DAVID); SOME DID NOT AND HE DID (JOB, JOSHUA, CALEB, ELIAKIM, ZERUBBABEL, DANIEL, HANANIAH MISHAEL AND AZARIAH, THE FORMER PROPHETS). THE SERVANT CENSUS — read before by topic in gen_27 (no-bearing there) — named, not fresh.')
srow(27, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOUR GREATNESS" — THIS IS THE PROTOTYPE FOR EVERY "YOUR GREATNESS" IN THE TORAH. ({SP_(27, 4, "זה", "בנין", "אב", "לכל", "גדלך", "שבתורה")} "this is the prototype for every \'your greatness\' in the Torah") — THE MIDDAH NAMED BY THE ROW: BINYAN AV (I3, the prototype) on the word; the ink: \'your greatness\' 3:24 and Joshua 3:7 — the Torah\'s one seat is the prototype of itself (the English: \'your goodness\' the sense).')
srow(27, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOUR STRONG HAND" — THESE ARE THE TEN PLAGUES THE HOLY ONE BROUGHT ON THE EGYPTIANS, OF WHICH "STRETCH OUT YOUR HAND" (Exodus 8:1) IS SAID. ({SP_(27, 5, "אלו", "עשר", "מכות", "שהביא", "הקדוש", "ברוך", "הוא")} "these are the ten plagues that the Holy One brought") — the strong hand as the plagues (the analogy of usage on \'hand\'); the ink: \'your strong hand\' 3:24 and Solomon\'s prayer.')
srow(27, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHAT GOD IS THERE IN HEAVEN OR EARTH" — NOT AS FLESH AND BLOOD: A GOVERNOR ON HIS PROVINCE FEARS HIS ASSESSOR WILL REVERSE HIM; YOU, WHO HAVE NO ASSESSOR, WHY DO YOU NOT PARDON ME? A KING ON HIS PLATFORM FEARS HIS DEPUTY; YOU, WHO HAVE NO DEPUTY, WHY NOT PARDON ME? ({SP_(27, 6, "אתה", "שאין", "לך", "סנקתידרוס", "מפני", "מה", "אין")} "you who have no assessor, why do you not") — the rhetorical question read as the plea\'s argument; the translation makes the same clause a confession (\'God whose Shekhinah is in heaven above and rules on earth\').')
srow(27, 7, 'CONTEXT', '"ACCORDING TO YOUR WORKS" — IN EGYPT; "AND YOUR MIGHTY ACTS" — AT THE SEA. ANOTHER WORD: — AT THE JORDAN. The hapax pair read as two theaters.')
srow(28, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"LET ME CROSS OVER, I PRAY, AND SEE" — COULD MOSES ASK TO ENTER THE LAND WHEN "YOU SHALL NOT CROSS THIS JORDAN" (3:27) WAS SAID? A PARABLE: THE KING DECREED THAT ONE SERVANT DRINK NO WINE THIRTY DAYS — I WILL NOT TASTE IT A YEAR, TWO YEARS — TO LIGHTEN HIS MASTER\'S WORD; TO THE SECOND — CAN I BE WITHOUT WINE ONE HOUR? — TO CHERISH HIS MASTER\'S WORD. SO MOSES CHERISHED THE OMNIPRESENT\'S WORD AND ASKED TO ENTER. ({SP_(28, 1, "כך", "משה", "היה", "מחבב", "דברי", "המקום")} "so Moses cherished the words of the Omnipresent") — the plea read as love of the decree, not defiance; the ink: \'let me cross, I pray\' three seats.')
srow(28, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"THAT GOOD HILL COUNTRY AND LEBANON" — ALL CALLED IT A MOUNTAIN: ABRAHAM ("ON THE MOUNTAIN OF THE LORD IT SHALL BE SEEN", Genesis 22:14), MOSES ("THAT GOOD HILL"), DAVID ("WHO SHALL ASCEND THE MOUNTAIN OF THE LORD", Psalm 24:3), ISAIAH ("THE MOUNTAIN OF THE HOUSE OF THE LORD", 2:2), THE NATIONS ("LET US GO UP TO THE MOUNTAIN OF THE LORD", 2:3). ({SP_(28, 2, "הכל", "קראו", "אותו", "הר")} "all called it a mountain") — \'that good hill\' (the ink: one seat) read as the Temple mount by five voices.')
srow(28, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND LEBANON" — LEBANON IS THE SANCTUARY ("GILEAD YOU ARE TO ME, THE HEAD OF LEBANON", Jeremiah 22:6; "LEBANON SHALL FALL BY A MIGHTY ONE", Isaiah 10:34); WHY LEBANON? IT WHITENS ISRAEL\'S SINS ("WHITE AS SNOW", Isaiah 1:18). ({SP_(28, 3, "מנין", "שאין", "לבנון", "אלא", "מקדש")} "whence that Lebanon is nothing but the sanctuary") — the reading of 6:2-3 repeated at 3:25, where THE TRANSLATION WRITES IT (\'the house of the sanctuary\' — the ink: three seats in Onkelos Deuteronomy).')
srow(29, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THE LORD WAS WROTH WITH ME FOR YOUR SAKES AND DID NOT HEAR ME" — R. ELIEZER: HE WAS FILLED WITH WRATH AGAINST ME; R. JOSHUA: LIKE A WOMAN WHO CANNOT BEND FOR HER PREGNANCY. ({SP_(29, 1, "כאשה", "שאינה", "יכולה", "לשוח", "מפני", "עברה")} "like a woman who cannot bend for her pregnancy") — the wrath-verb\'s hitpael (the ink: nine tokens) read by R. Joshua from the same consonants as pregnancy; the store\'s \'and-cross-over\' the third homograph.')
srow(29, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"FOR YOUR SAKES" — ON YOUR ACCOUNT THIS WAS DONE TO ME. "AND DID NOT HEAR ME" — DID NOT ACCEPT MY PRAYER. "AND THE LORD SAID TO ME: ENOUGH FOR YOU" — MOSES, WHEN A MAN VOWS, WHERE DOES HE GO? TO HIS MASTER TO RELEASE HIS VOW. WHAT IS ON YOU? TO HEAR YOUR MASTER\'S WORD! ({SP_(29, 2, "ולא", "קבל", "תפלתי")} "and he did not accept my prayer"; {SP_(29, 2, "לשמוע", "דברי", "רבך")} "to hear the words of your master") — \'enough\' read by its sound (\'your master\' — rav); THE TRANSLATION\'S \'did not accept from me\' matches the Sifrei\'s gloss word for word (the ink: 1:45 and 3:26 the same Aramaic).')
srow(29, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "ENOUGH FOR YOU" — MOSES, YOU ARE AN EXAMPLE TO THE JUDGES: IF MOSES, WISEST OF THE WISE, WAS SHOWN NO FAVOR FOR "HEAR NOW, REBELS" (Numbers 20:10) AND BARRED FROM THE LAND, THOSE WHO DELAY AND PERVERT JUDGMENT HOW MUCH MORE! AND IF MOSES, TOLD "ENOUGH, NO MORE", DID NOT CEASE TO ASK MERCY, OTHER MEN HOW MUCH MORE! HEZEKIAH, TOLD "SET YOUR HOUSE IN ORDER, YOU SHALL DIE" (2 Kings 20:1), DID NOT CEASE — EVEN WITH A SHARP SWORD ON HIS NECK LET A MAN NOT WITHHOLD HIMSELF FROM MERCY (Isaiah 38:2). ({SP_(29, 3, "אפלו", "חרב", "חדה", "על", "צוארו", "של", "אדם")} "even a sharp sword on a man\'s neck") — two a-fortioris (I1): the judges\' example, prayer never withheld.')
srow(29, 4, 'CONTEXT', 'ANOTHER WORD: "ENOUGH FOR YOU" — MUCH IS KEPT FOR YOU WITH ME IN THE WORLD TO COME, AS ONE SAYS: I HAVE MUCH FOR YOU, DO NOT SHAME ME. ANOTHER: AS ONE SAYS: SO-AND-SO HAS CROSSED THE LINE WITH SO-AND-SO. The third and fourth readings of \'enough\'.')
srow(29, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"SPEAK NO MORE TO ME... GO UP TO THE TOP OF PISGAH" (3:26-27) — R. ELIEZER BEN JACOB: ONE PRAYER IS BETTER THAN A HUNDRED GOOD DEEDS: FOR ALL MOSES\' DEEDS HE WAS NOT TOLD "GO UP", FOR THIS HE WAS. HENCE: THOSE OUTSIDE THE LAND TURN TOWARD THE LAND (1 Kings 8:48), IN THE LAND TOWARD JERUSALEM (2 Chronicles 6:34), IN JERUSALEM TOWARD THE TEMPLE (6:32), IN THE TEMPLE TOWARD THE HOLY OF HOLIES (6:26) — NORTH FACES SOUTH, SOUTH NORTH, EAST WEST, WEST EAST: ALL ISRAEL PRAYS TOWARD ONE PLACE. THE DIRECTIONS OF PRAYER ({SP_(29, 5, "נמצאו", "כל", "ישראל", "מתפללים", "למקום", "אחד")} "so all Israel is found praying toward one place") — 3:27\'s four directions (west, north, south, east — the ink\'s order against Genesis 13:14\'s) become the compass of prayer; the compile\'s docket: the four directions as the register of \'lift up your eyes\'.')
srow(29, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND SEE WITH YOUR EYES" — A PARABLE: THE KING DECREED HIS SON NOT ENTER HIS BEDCHAMBER; AT THE PALACE GATE HE DREW HIM AND SPOKE; AT THE HALL DOOR; AT THE BEDCHAMBER: FROM HERE YOU ARE FORBIDDEN. SO MOSES: I AM KEPT FROM THE LAND ONLY THE WIDTH OF THIS JORDAN, A ROPE OF FIFTY CUBITS! — "SEE WITH YOUR EYES, FOR YOU SHALL NOT CROSS". ({SP_(29, 6, "מלא", "חבל", "של", "חמשים", "אמה")} "the fullness of a rope of fifty cubits") — the Jordan measured at fifty cubits by the Sifrei (a number the text does not carry: the compile\'s docket flags it as the shelf\'s measure, not the ink\'s).')
srow(29, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND CHARGE JOSHUA" — CHARGING IS URGING ("MOSES CALLED JOSHUA... BE STRONG AND OF GOOD COURAGE", 31:7) — STRONG IN TORAH, OF GOOD COURAGE IN GOOD DEEDS. ({SP_(29, 7, "אין", "צואה", "אלא", "זרוז")} "charging is nothing but urging") — the charge-verb fixed from 31:7 (E7); \'strong / of good courage\' split between Torah and deeds.')
srow(29, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'"FOR HE SHALL CROSS BEFORE THIS PEOPLE" — IF HE CROSSES BEFORE THEM THEY CROSS, IF NOT, NOT. ({SP_(29, 8, "אם", "עובר", "לפניהם", "עוברים")} "if he crosses before them, they cross") — the condition read from \'before\': the compile\'s rule for Joshua (the crossing gated on the leader).')
srow(29, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND HE SHALL CAUSE THEM TO INHERIT" — IF HE GIVES THEM INHERITANCE THEY INHERIT, IF NOT, NOT. SO AT AI: THIRTY-SIX RIGHTEOUS FELL ("THE MEN OF AI SMOTE ABOUT THIRTY-SIX", Joshua 7:5-10); JOSHUA TORE HIS CLOTHES AND FELL — "RISE, WHY DO YOU FALL ON YOUR FACE? DID I NOT SAY TO MOSES YOUR MASTER: IF HE CROSSES THEY CROSS, IF HE GIVES THEY INHERIT? YOU SENT THEM AND DID NOT GO AFTER THEM!" THE AI ROW ({SP_(29, 9, "שלחתם", "ולא", "הלכת", "אחריהם")} "you sent them and did not go after them") — Joshua 7 read as the breach of 3:28\'s rule: the run\'s failure traced to the spec (THE RUN AGAINST THE SPEC — the sitting\'s clearest link, taught by the Sifrei: LR1).')
srow(30, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND WE DWELT IN THE VALLEY" — HE SAID: WHAT MADE US DWELL IN THE VALLEY? THE EVIL DEEDS WE DID AT PEOR! The head row on 3:29 ({SP_(30, 1, "מעשים", "רעים", "שעשינו", "בפעור")} "evil deeds that we did at Peor") — the valley read as the place of the sin (Numbers 25 — the walk\'s num_25_peor_pinchas): the span opens with the places as sins (1:1) and closes on one (3:29); the ink: \'opposite Beth-peor\' three seats, Moses\' grave the third.')
srow(30, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: SEE THE DIFFERENCE BETWEEN YOU AND ME — HOW MANY PRAYERS AND ENTREATIES I MADE, AND IT WAS DECREED I NOT ENTER; BUT YOU ANGERED HIM FORTY YEARS ("FORTY YEARS I LOATHED THAT GENERATION", Psalm 95:10), AND THE GREATEST OF YOU BOWED TO PEOR — AND HIS RIGHT HAND IS STRETCHED OUT TO RECEIVE THE PENITENT: "AND NOW, ISRAEL, HEAR THE STATUTES" (4:1) — YOU ARE NEW, THE PAST IS FORGIVEN. THE SPAN\'S LAST ROW ({SP_(30, 2, "וימינו", "פשוטה", "לקבל", "שבים")} "and his right hand is stretched out to receive the penitent"): the Sifrei crosses from 3:29 into 4:1 — the rebuke\'s close as forgiveness; the next reading (chapter 4) opens where this row points.')
assert sorted(S) == [(p, r) for p in range(26, 31) for r in range(1, SIF_ROWS[p] + 1)], sorted(S)
